  "source_ref": "Two-hop join: Sundance EMC2-DP Design Specification QCF51 Issue 3.3.0 section 8 \"FMC Pin-Out\" (carrier FMC position -> Trenz B2B pins JB1-JB3; coordinate-extracted, byte-identical doc shared by all EMC2 variants) joined to Trenz TE0841 schematic SCH-TE0841-03 (41I31-A variant; B2B-Connectors sheet 5 JM1-JM3 pin -> net, FPGA U1 symbol sheets net -> XCKU040-SFVA784 ball; balls sanity-checked against the AMD xcku040sfva784 package file). The TE0841 module inverts pair polarity on most LA pairs (29 of 31) and on GBTCLK0 (P position lands on MGTREFCLK0N_225 Y5, N on Y6) - intentional routing, actual copper recorded. EXCLUDED: DP0 (QCF51 wires the DP0_C2M positions C2/C3 to the module GTH RX3 P2/P1 and DP0_M2C positions C6/C7 to GTH TX3 R4/R3 - host TX/RX swapped relative to VITA 57.1, so a compliant card cannot use DP0; left absent so the closed-world join reads incompatible). EXCLUDED LA30/LA32/LA33: QCF51 maps them to JB2.90-99, which on the TE0841 are the module JTAG block and GND (91=REF_JTAG 3.3V, 93=TMS, 95=TDI, 97=TDO, 99=TCK, 90=GND) - not FPGA I/O on this module variant; caution: an FMC card driving LA30/32/33 would drive the module JTAG pins. EXCLUDED LA11_P: its B2B pin JB1.39 is tied to the TE0841 PL_1V8 power rail (LA11_N recorded alone at AH12 via module net B64_L5_N; the LA11 pair is unusable differentially). EXCLUDED SCL/SDA: JB1.32 -> module net SC1 (system-controller, no FPGA ball; JB1.34 unconnected). FMC JTAG -> carrier chain, GA0/GA1 not B2B-routed. PRSNT_M2C_L reaches PL ball F8 (B68_L24_P). Carrier-side population not verifiable (no EMC2 carrier schematic cached); module-side routes are direct per schematic.",
